# Build context for deploy/Dockerfile (the api and worker image).
#
# input/ alone is hundreds of MB of client Excel containing customer PII. It must
# never enter a build context — that is slow, and it would bake client data into
# an image layer where it is very hard to remove.
#
# EVERY PATTERN HERE IS `**/`-PREFIXED, and that is not decoration. Docker anchors
# an unprefixed pattern at the CONTEXT ROOT, while git matches the same spelling at
# any depth. compose builds these images with `context: ..`, so a bare `input/`
# excluded <root>/input/ and silently did NOT exclude deploy/input/ — which held 40
# real client Shopee exports, 382 MB, shipped to the daemon on every build. Git had
# been ignoring that directory the whole time, which is exactly why nobody noticed.
# Measured 2026-08-17 with a mimic build; see M6-PLAN.md phase 0.
**/input/
**/output/
**/artifacts/
**/.scratch/
**/.uploads/

.git/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# The web app has its own image and its own build context.
web/node_modules/
web/.next/

# The team-owned .xlsb master is mounted at runtime, never baked in — a stale
# copy would silently diverge from the team's own rules (D8).
config/*.xlsb

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
